-- title:
--   Divisibility between toric subgroups of the Néron object at p
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ lying in the nonunits of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for these data — that is, a structure morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{base}\ p$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ over $\mathrm{base}\ p$ carrying a relative group law, and identifications of the $\mathrm{genPt}$-points of $X$ with $J_H(M/p)$ at the induced level and of its $(\mathrm{resPt}\ A \circ \sigma_A)$-points with $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the reduction — and let $O$ be a `JHNeronObjectAtP` over $\Lambda$: a smooth, separated, surjective group scheme over $\mathrm{base}\ p$ with commutative relative group law, an additive identification of its $\mathrm{genPt}$-points with $J_H(M)$ that is Galois- and Hecke-equivariant, flatness and surjectivity of multiplication by each positive integer, together with the remaining toric data of the structure. Let $m, d$ be positive integers. Then for every $y$ in `O.toricPts m`, the subgroup of $J_H(M)$ generated by the range of `O.toricPoint m`, there exists $z$ in `O.toricPts (m * d)` with $d \cdot z = y$.
--
--   This records that the toric subgroups attached to the Néron object of $J_H(M)$ at a place above $p$, with $p \mid M$, form a tower in which each level is divisible by $d$ into the level multiplied by $d$; it reflects the surjectivity of $\zeta \mapsto \zeta^d$ on roots of unity in the character groups of the toric parts. It is used in the assembly of the monodromy/toric comparison at level $\Gamma_H(M)$, namely by [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner).
